## Part 7. Quick glossary

| Term | Plain meaning |
| --- | --- |
| SST | Sea surface temperature, the warmth of the ocean's top layer |
| ENSO | The El Niño and La Niña seesaw in the tropical Pacific |
| El Niño | The warm phase; La Niña is the cold phase |
| Niño 3.4 | The specific equatorial Pacific box used to measure it |
| Anomaly | How far a value is from normal for that time of year |
| Climatology | The many year average you subtract to get an anomaly |
| ONI | The official three month averaged index that defines El Niño |
| CNN | A neural network built to read grid or image data |
| Channel | One layer of a stacked input; here, one input month |
| Persistence | The dumb baseline that assumes no change |
| Leakage | Accidentally letting the model see test answers |
| Skill | How much you beat the baseline by |
| netCDF | The file format the ocean data comes in |
| ONNX | A portable model format that runs without full PyTorch |
| Reanalysis | Model plus observations blended into a gap free weather history (what ERA5 and Open-Meteo give you) |

